From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 21:05:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] media: apple: avd: don't overrun the SRAM ring at the
 counter wrap

The queue firmware transport streams program words through a ring in the
CM3's SRAM. Host and firmware count words with free-running u32 counters
and both place word n at n % ring_words, but the ring holds 6144 words,
which does not divide 2^32: the lap that ends at the wrap has only 4096
slots, and the next one starts again at slot 0. While the writer has
wrapped and the reader has not, the free space computed from the counters
counts the 2048 slots that lap skipped, so the host can write over words
of the old lap that are not read yet.

Take those slots off the free space while the reader is behind the wrap.
A write that fits still crosses it (the split test keeps passing); a host
test now puts the reader at slot 3000 of the last lap and checks that the
writer stops before it.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
---
 .../media/platform/apple/avd/avd-backend-queue.c    | 13 +++++++++++++
 .../media/platform/apple/avd/tests/program-test.py  | 11 +++++++++++
 2 files changed, 24 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/apple/avd/avd-backend-queue.c b/drivers/media/platform/apple/avd/avd-backend-queue.c
index 36ae764906..bec03920c2 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/apple/avd/avd-backend-queue.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/apple/avd/avd-backend-queue.c
@@ -284,6 +284,19 @@ static int avd_qfw_stream(struct avd_dev *avd, const u32 *words, u32 count)
 		if (used > q->ring_words)
 			return -EIO;
 		space = q->ring_words - used;
+		/*
+		 * Both sides place word n at n % ring_words, and ring_words does
+		 * not divide 2^32: the lap that ends at the counter wrap has only
+		 * 2^32 % ring_words slots, and the next lap starts again at slot 0.
+		 * While the writer has wrapped and the reader has not, the slots
+		 * that lap skipped do not separate them.
+		 */
+		if (rp > q->wp) {
+			u32 skip = (q->ring_words - (u32)((1ULL << 32) % q->ring_words)) %
+				   q->ring_words;
+
+			space = space > skip ? space - skip : 0;
+		}
 		if (!space) {
 			if (time_after(jiffies, timeout))
 				return -ETIMEDOUT;
diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/apple/avd/tests/program-test.py b/drivers/media/platform/apple/avd/tests/program-test.py
index 6a0f353e4a..16c637a9a1 100755
--- a/drivers/media/platform/apple/avd/tests/program-test.py
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/apple/avd/tests/program-test.py
@@ -336,6 +336,17 @@ int main(int argc, char **argv)
   assert(q.wp==(u32)(start+32));
   for(unsigned int i=0;i<32;i++)assert(readl(q.sram+4*((u32)(start+i)%0x1800))==words[i]);
  }
+ /* After the u32 wrap, the reader still in the short last lap (slot 3000):
+  * the writer may fill slots 0-2999 only, not the 2048 slots that lap skipped. */
+ {
+  static u32 many[3100];u32 rp=(u32)(0x100000000ULL-4096+3000);
+  for(unsigned int i=0;i<3100;i++)many[i]=0x56780000U+i;
+  memset(q.sram,0,0x10000);writel(0xdeadbeef,q.sram+4*3000);
+  q.wp=0;writel(rp,q.sram+0x7ff8);
+  assert(avd_qfw_stream(&dev,many,3100)==-ETIMEDOUT);
+  assert(q.wp==3000);
+  assert(readl(q.sram+4*2999)==many[2999]&&readl(q.sram+4*3000)==0xdeadbeef);
+ }
  /* A sole fatal completion must keep DMA buffers owned until reset. */
  memset(q.sram,0,0x10000);jiffies=123;
  dev.frames[0].tag=0x10;dev.frames[0].state=AVD_FRAME_SUBMITTED;
-- 
2.43.0

